ll="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" transform="matrix(0.6 0.0 0.0 0.6 12.52 171.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.08em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="9.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.07)" width="10.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.SS2.p4.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" color="#FF0000" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" transform="matrix(0.6 0.0 0.0 0.6 12.52 186.9)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.08em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="9.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.07)" width="10.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.SS2.p4.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" color="#FF0000" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" transform="matrix(0.6 0.0 0.0 0.6 12.52 202.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.08em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="9.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.07)" width="10.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.SS2.p4.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Our starting point</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><math id="S5.SSx4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 11</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S5.SSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The strategy fails for <math id="S5.SSx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 11</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="S5.SSx4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,11}</annotation></semantics></math> has a holomorphic differential form (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, Section 2.3]</cite>). By a Theorem of Roĭtman <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>, this implies that <math id="S5.SSx4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})</annotation></semantics></math> is uncountable for <math id="S5.SSx4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 11</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="S5.SSx4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})\neq R_{0}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})\neq R_{0}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SSx4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 11</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Genus 2 and hyperelliptic curves in general</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, we computed the Chow rings of moduli stacks <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Hyp}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Hyp}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> of smooth pointed hyperelliptic curves of genus <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 2g+6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 2g+6</annotation></semantics></math> marked points.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Corollary 1.1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)<span id="S6.Thmthm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 2g+6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 2g+6</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathrm{Hyp}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathrm{Hyp}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> classes.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:155.3pt;">
<p id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, we see that <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{2,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{2,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives the new blue column of open circles in the first chart to the right. Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Filling criterion, version 1). ‣ 4. Filling criteria ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and the results of Section <a href="#S5" title="5. Genus 
        
          0
        
       and 
        
          1 ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> immediately allow us to fill in the circles with <math id="S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 8</annotation></semantics></math>.
However,
because <math id="S6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n}</annotation></semantics></math> does <em id="S6.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> have <math id="S6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 11</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Filling criterion, version 1). ‣ 4. Filling criteria ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>(3) fails for filling in <math id="S6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 9</annotation></semantics></math>. To fill <math id="S6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,9}</annotation></semantics></math>, we require an extension of Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Corollary 1.1 of []). ‣ 6. Genus 2 and hyperelliptic curves in general ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> to a partial compactification of <math id="S6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Hyp}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Hyp}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which was also proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
<p id="S6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{g,n}\subseteq\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{g,n}\subseteq\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the moduli stack parametrizing irreducible nodal hyperelliptic curves of genus <math id="S6.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> marked points. The argument in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> provided a</p>
</div>
