<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">stratification of <math id="S6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> into spaces that we claim satisfy the CKgP.
This is clear from considering <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, Equations 4.10 and 4.12]</cite>
once we know that <math id="S6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{BPU}\cong\mathrm{B}(\mathbb{G}_{m}\ltimes\mathbb{G}_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>BPU</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋉</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{BPU}\cong\mathrm{B}(\mathbb{G}_{m}\ltimes\mathbb{G}_{a})</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP. To see this, note that <math id="S6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{B}\mathbb{G}_{m}\to\mathrm{BPU}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>BPU</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{B}\mathbb{G}_{m}\to\mathrm{BPU}</annotation></semantics></math> is an affine bundle (see proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, Lemma 4.6]</cite>). Then apply Lemmas <a href="#S3.Thmthm5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.1. Basic lemmas ‣ 3. The Chow–Künneth generation property ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 3.8. ‣ 3.1. Basic lemmas ‣ 3. The Chow–Künneth generation property ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.2</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 1.1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)<span id="S6.Thmthm2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 2g+6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 2g+6</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{I}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{I}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> classes and the boundary divisor parametrizing irreducible, nodal hyperelliptic curves. Moreover, <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We now proceed using version 2 of the Filling criteria.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.3</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 9</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}\smallsetminus\Delta_{\mathrm{dn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>dn</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}\smallsetminus\Delta_{\mathrm{dn}}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and the CKgP. Hence, <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and the CKgP for <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 9</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each of the graphs in the stable graph stratification of <math id="S6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}\smallsetminus\Delta_{\mathrm{dn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>dn</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}\smallsetminus\Delta_{\mathrm{dn}}</annotation></semantics></math> fits into one of the following four categories:</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Graphs where all vertices have genus <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. All classes supported here are tautological and these strata have CKgP by Section <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1. Genus 
          
            0 ‣ 5. Genus 
        
          0
        
       and 
        
          1 ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One genus <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> vertex and one genus <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> vertex with two edges between them.
There are <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> marked points coming out of the genus <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> vertex and <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}=n-n_{0}\leq 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}=n-n_{0}\leq 8</annotation></semantics></math> marked points coming out of the genus <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> vertex.
This is the graph for (gluing twice)</p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,n_{0}+2}\times\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n_{1}+2}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,n_{0}+2}\times\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n_{1}+2}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}+2\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}+2\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math>, so these strata have CKgP and contribute only tautological classes by Sections <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1. Genus 
          
            0 ‣ 5. Genus 
        
          0
        
       and 
        
          1 ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> and <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2. Genus 
          
            1 ‣ 5. Genus 
        
          0
        
       and 
        
          1 ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One vertex of genus <math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> with self edge and <math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> marked points.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One vertex of genus <math id="S6.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> marked points.</p>
</div></li>
</ol><img src="2208.02357v2/SamsStableGraphs3.png" id="S6.p5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="499" height="101" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
<p id="S6.p5.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Examples of stable graphs of types (1)–(4).</p>
<p id="S6.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the union of strata of type (3) and (4) is <math id="S6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{2,n}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{2,n}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we are done by Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 6.2 (Theorem 1.1 of []). ‣ 6. Genus 2 and hyperelliptic curves in general ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=2</annotation></semantics></math>, Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Corollary 1.1 of []). ‣ 6. Genus 2 and hyperelliptic curves in general ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>
tells us <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{2,10})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{2,10})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{2,10})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{2,10})</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we have <em id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> proved that <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,10})=R^{*}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,10})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,10})=R^{*}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,10})</annotation></semantics></math> because we have not been able to prove that cycles supported on the boundary stratum for
<math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,11}\times\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,11}\times\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math> are tautological. We think it likely that many non-tautological <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-cycles are supported on this stratum.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7. </span>Plane curves</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we give a quotient stack presentation for stacks of smooth pointed plane curves of degree <math id="S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the presentation to show that the Chow rings of these stacks have the CKgP and are generated by restrictions of tautological classes from <math id="S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we will finish the <math id="S7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=3</annotation></semantics></math> cases of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 1.4. ‣ 1.2. Statement of main result ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a> because nonhyperelliptic curves of genus <math id="S7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> are plane quartics.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1. </span>Construction of the stack</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we define the stack of pointed plane curves. Let <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> be a positive integer and set <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:={d-1\choose 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:={d-1\choose 2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the stack whose objects over a scheme <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> are given by commutative diagrams</p>
<table id="S7.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S7.Ex1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="67.54" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-32.04px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 142.24 67.54" width="142.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,67.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(89.04,0) translate(0,32.04)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -53.2 -26.97)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 64.07)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.52)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(18.32,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -12.36 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="10.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces C}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 36.63 0) translate(51.49,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -12.32 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="10.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces P}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 59.01)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0.8 0) translate(17.52,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -11.56 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.67em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces S}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -14.3 20.98 L 15.81 20.98"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -14.3 20.98)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 2.71 C 0.95 2.71 1.72 2.1 1.72 1.36 C 1.72 0.61 0.95 0 0 0"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.09 20.98)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -2.53 26.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.46em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.41)" width="5.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces j}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -34.88 12.18 L -34.88 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -34.88 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -31.63 -2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="6.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces f}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 21.11 12.18 L -16.63 -11.88"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-0.8433 -0.53745 0.53745 -0.8433 -16.87 -12.03)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.26 -7.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="6.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -41.43 -12.18 C -45.69 -3.65 -45.22 4.22 -40.27 11.71"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.55107 0.83446 -0.83446 0.55107 -40.11 11.95)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -86.06 5.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.78)" width="38.54"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
