<p id="S7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:C\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:C\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth proper relative curve with <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> pairwise disjoint sections <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n}:S\rightarrow C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n}:S\rightarrow C</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:P\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:P\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> fibration; and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j:C\hookrightarrow P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j:C\hookrightarrow P</annotation></semantics></math> is a closed embedding such that for every geometric point <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{s}\hookrightarrow\mathbb{P}^{2}_{\kappa(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{s}\hookrightarrow\mathbb{P}^{2}_{\kappa(s)}</annotation></semantics></math> is of degree <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. The morphisms in <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{d,n}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{d,n}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> between objects <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(C\rightarrow P\rightarrow S,\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n}:S\rightarrow C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C\rightarrow P\rightarrow S,\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n}:S\rightarrow C)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S7.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(C^{\prime}\rightarrow P^{\prime}\rightarrow S,\sigma_{1}^{\prime},\dots,\sigma_{n}^{\prime}:S\rightarrow C^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C^{\prime}\rightarrow P^{\prime}\rightarrow S,\sigma_{1}^{\prime},\dots,\sigma_{n}^{\prime}:S\rightarrow C^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> are isomorphisms <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\rightarrow P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\rightarrow P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> inducing isomorphisms <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\rightarrow C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\rightarrow C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> sending the sections <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>, Landesman shows that the natural map <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{d,0}\to\mathcal{M}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{d,0}\to\mathcal{M}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is a locally closed embedding of stacks when <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking the base change along <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\to\mathcal{M}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\to\mathcal{M}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>,
it follows that <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{d,n}\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{d,n}\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a locally closed embedding for any <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The stack <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a natural morphism to <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BPGL_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BPGL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BPGL_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, sending the family of plane curves to its associated <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-fibration. We define the stack <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> by the following Cartesian diagram:</p>
<table id="S7.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
