<p id="S7.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The stack <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>-banded gerbe over <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{F}_{d,n})\cong A^{*}(\mathcal{G}_{d,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{F}_{d,n})\cong A^{*}(\mathcal{G}_{d,n})</annotation></semantics></math>, as we always work with rational coefficients, and <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies CKgP if and only if <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> does (Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm6" title="Lemma 3.6. ‣ 3.1. Basic lemmas ‣ 3. The Chow–Künneth generation property ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>). The points of <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> over a scheme <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> are given by diagrams</p>
<table id="S7.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

