<p id="S7.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with trivial first Chern class. The universal bundle <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is pulled back from the universal bundle over <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BSL_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BSL_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We construct <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, for certain values of <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> depending on <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, explicitly, and use the explicit presentation to describe its Chow ring.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}\rightarrow\BSL_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}\rightarrow\BSL_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, the universal <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle. Let <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the fiber product of <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}\rightarrow\BSL_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}\rightarrow\BSL_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. There are projection maps <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}:(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}\rightarrow\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}:(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}\rightarrow\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{d}:=\gamma^{*}\gamma_{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d)=\gamma^{*}\Sym^{d}\mathcal{V}^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{d}:=\gamma^{*}\gamma_{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d)=\gamma^{*}\Sym^{d}\mathcal{V}^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have an evaluation map</p>
<table id="S7.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{d}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{d}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}^{*}\mathcal{W}_{d}\cong\eta_{j}^{*}\mathcal{W}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}^{*}\mathcal{W}_{d}\cong\eta_{j}^{*}\mathcal{W}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is by definition a pullback from <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BSL_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BSL_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will denote this pullback by <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{d}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{d}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have a direct sum evaluation map</p>
<table id="S7.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{d}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}}\rightarrow\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}\eta_{i}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{d}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}}\rightarrow\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}\eta_{i}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the preimage of the zero section under (<a href="#S7.E1" title="In 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>). The stack <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizes tuples <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,p_{1},\dots,p_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,p_{1},\dots,p_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is a degree <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> form in <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle with trivial first Chern class, and <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\dots,p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\dots,p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are (not necessarily distinct) points such that <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The stack <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is not a vector bundle over <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> because the fiber dimension jumps when the points <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> fail to impose independent conditions on degree <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> curves.
In order to study the Chow ring of <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we will need to understand when (<a href="#S7.E1" title="In 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>) is surjective. By cohomology and base change, we can check surjectivity on the fibers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.1</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset\mathbb{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset\mathbb{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be a collection of <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3d-1</annotation></semantics></math> distinct points. Suppose there is an irreducible nodal plane curve <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset\mathbb{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset\mathbb{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the smooth locus of <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the evaluation map</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{2},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d))\rightarrow H^{0}(\Gamma,\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{\Gamma})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{2},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d))\rightarrow H^{0}(\Gamma,\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{\Gamma})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is surjective.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The evaluation map factors as</span></p>
<table id="S7.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{2},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d))\to H^{0}(C,\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{C})\to H^{0}(\Gamma,\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{\Gamma})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{2},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d))\to H^{0}(C,\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{C})\to H^{0}(\Gamma,\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{\Gamma}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The first map in (<a href="#S7.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>) is surjective because <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{2},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{2},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. So it remains to show that the second map is surjective. To do so, consider the exact sequence</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{C}(-\Gamma)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{\Gamma}\rightarrow 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{C}(-\Gamma)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{\Gamma}\rightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">After taking global sections, it suffices to show that <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{C}(-\Gamma))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(d)|_{C}(-\Gamma))=0</annotation></semantics></math>. By Serre duality, this is equivalent to showing that <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(-d)|_{C}\otimes\omega_{C}(\Gamma))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(-d)|_{C}\otimes\omega_{C}(\Gamma))=0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the dualizing sheaf, which is a line bundle of degree <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g-2</annotation></semantics></math>. The bundle <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(-d)|_{C}\otimes\omega_{C}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{2}}(-d)|_{C}\otimes\omega_{C}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is of degree</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-d^{2}+2g-2+n=-d^{2}+(d-1)(d-2)-2+n=-3d+n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-d^{2}+2g-2+n=-d^{2}+(d-1)(d-2)-2+n=-3d+n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">On an irreducible curve, a line bundle of negative degree has no global sections. Hence, this line bundle has no global sections when <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3d-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the locus over which (<a href="#S7.E1" title="In 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>) is surjective.
Note that <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is necessarily contained in the complement of the diagonals in <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{d,n}:=Y_{d,n}|_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{d,n}:=Y_{d,n}|_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the kernel of (<a href="#S7.E1" title="In 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>) restricted to <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle over <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. The projectivization <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizes tuples <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,V,p_{1},\dots,p_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,V,p_{1},\dots,p_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a degree <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> curve in <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V</annotation></semantics></math> containing the points <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\dots,p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\dots,p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and this collection of points imposes independent conditions on polynomials of degree <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 7.1. ‣ 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a> says that the image of <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S7.SS1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3d-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.2</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The stack <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP for <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3d-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have a sequence of morphisms</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\rightarrow U\subset(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}\rightarrow\BSL_{3}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\rightarrow U\subset(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}\rightarrow\BSL_{3},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where each <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\subset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\subset</annotation></semantics></math> is an open embedding and each <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> is a (product of) projective bundles. Thus, <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP by Lemmas <a href="#S3.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Basic lemmas ‣ 3. The Chow–Künneth generation property ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmthm7" title="Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.1. Basic lemmas ‣ 3. The Chow–Künneth generation property ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2. </span>Generators for the Chow ring</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Chow ring of <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BSL_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BSL_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by
the Chern classes of the tautological rank <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> bundle <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}(\mathcal{V}),c_{3}(\mathcal{V})\in A^{*}(\BSL_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}(\mathcal{V}),c_{3}(\mathcal{V})\in A^{*}(\BSL_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the projective bundle theorem, the Chow ring of <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated over <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\BSL_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\BSL_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> by the classes of the relative <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>’s.
Let <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}:(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}\to\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}:(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n}\to\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\mathrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>th</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\mathrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> projection and write <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=\eta_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(1))\in A^{1}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=\eta_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(1))\in A^{1}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V})^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the projective bundle theorem again, the Chow ring of <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated over <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(U)</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta:=c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}}(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta:=c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}}(1))</annotation></semantics></math>. In summary, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.3</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The ring <math id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathbb{P}K_{d,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathbb{P}K_{d,n})</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{G}_{d,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{G}_{d,n})</annotation></semantics></math>, is generated by (the pullbacks of)</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}(V),\qquad c_{3}(V),\qquad z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\qquad\text{and}\qquad\zeta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}(V),\qquad c_{3}(V),\qquad z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\qquad\text{and}\qquad\zeta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to give a geometric interpretation of these generators, we first construct the universal pointed plane curve over <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. By an abuse of notation, we will continue to denote by <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> the pullback of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BSL_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BSL_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we consider the diagram</p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S7.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="75.52" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-37.4px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 205.98 75.52" width="205.98"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,75.52) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(102.99,0) translate(0,37.4)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -102.99 -28.38)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 74.79)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.52)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(70.53,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -64.57 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.49em;font-size:10pt;" height="16.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="129.15"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{P}:=\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\times_{\BSL_{3}}\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{P}:=\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\times_{\BSL_{3}}\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 141.06 0) translate(49.06,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -9.9 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="19.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS2.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 65.78)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 43.36 0) translate(27.17,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -21.21 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="42.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS2.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 38.35 26.34 L 70.45 26.34"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 70.73 26.34)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 48.74 30.98)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="11.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS2.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -32.46 10.77 L -32.46 -13.03"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -32.46 -13.3)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -29.2 -2.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="11.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS2.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We have a morphism of bundles on <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S7.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}}(-1)\otimes\pi_{2}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(-d)\rightarrow K_{d,n}\otimes\pi_{2}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(-d)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}}(-1)\otimes\pi_{2}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(-d)\rightarrow K_{d,n}\otimes\pi_{2}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(-d)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the first map arises from the tautological sequence on <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> and the second is obtained from multiplying forms. This morphism defines a sheaf of ideals in <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we will denote by <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\subset\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\subset\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> the corresponding divisor. By construction, the restriction of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a relative plane curve <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathcal{C}\rightarrow\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathcal{C}\rightarrow\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, we show that it has <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> sections.
The product of the identity map together with the composition</p>
<table id="S7.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\rightarrow U\hookrightarrow(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}\xrightarrow{\eta_{i}}\mathbb{P}V," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">η</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mover><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\rightarrow U\hookrightarrow(\mathbb{P}V)^{n}\xrightarrow{\eta_{i}}\mathbb{P}V,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">induces a section of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S7.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}:\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\to\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\times_{\BSL_{3}}\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}=\mathcal{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}:\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\to\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}\times_{\BSL_{3}}\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}=\mathcal{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">These sections factor through <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> by the definition of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, the fiber of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\ldots,p_{n})\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\ldots,p_{n})\in U</annotation></semantics></math> is the space of degree <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> forms <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> vanishing at the <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the fiber of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> over a degree <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> form <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is the vanishing of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the locus over which <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth. Let <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the open locus over which <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is stable (so, of course, <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,n}\subseteq X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,n}\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.4</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3d-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>.
The generators <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}(\mathcal{V}),c_{3}(\mathcal{V}),z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}(\mathcal{V}),c_{3}(\mathcal{V}),z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathbb{P}K_{d,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathbb{P}K_{d,n})</annotation></semantics></math> restrict to polynomials in the <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> classes on <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{G}_{d,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{G}_{d,n})</annotation></semantics></math> are generated by pullbacks of tautological classes.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have the universal diagram restricted to <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S7.Ex13.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="67.54" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-32.04px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 141.68 67.54" width="141.68"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,67.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(88.34,0) translate(0,32.04)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -53.34 -26.97)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 64.07)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.52)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 1.28 0) translate(17.87,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -11.92 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.99"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex13.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 38.3 0) translate(50.79,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -11.63 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex13.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 59.01)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(19.15,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.19 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="12.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex13.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces X}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -14.05 20.98 L 17.34 20.98"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -14.05 20.98)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 2.71 C 0.95 2.71 1.72 2.1 1.72 1.36 C 1.72 0.61 0.95 0 0 0"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.62 20.98)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -1.64 26.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.46em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.41)" width="5.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex13.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces j}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -34.19 12.18 L -34.19 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -34.19 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -30.93 -2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="6.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex13.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces f}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 21.92 12.18 L -15.9 -11.88"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-0.8438 -0.53667 0.53667 -0.8438 -16.14 -12.03)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 6.03 -7.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="6.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex13.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -40.73 -12.18 C -45 -3.65 -44.52 4.22 -39.57 11.71"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.55107 0.83446 -0.83446 0.55107 -39.42 11.95)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -85.36 5.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.78)" width="38.54"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex13.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}}(1)|_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}K_{d,n}}(1)|_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By construction, <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the zero locus of a section of <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By adjunction and the fact that <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle with trivial first Chern class,</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{f}=j^{*}(\omega_{\pi}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d)\otimes\pi^{*}\mathcal{O}_{X}(1))=f^{*}\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)\otimes j^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d-3)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{f}=j^{*}(\omega_{\pi}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d)\otimes\pi^{*}\mathcal{O}_{X}(1))=f^{*}\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)\otimes j^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d-3).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Pushing forward by <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{*}\omega_{f}=\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)\otimes\pi_{*}j_{*}j^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}V}(d-3)=\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)\otimes\Sym^{d-3}\mathcal{V}^{\vee}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{*}\omega_{f}=\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)\otimes\pi_{*}j_{*}j^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}V}(d-3)=\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)\otimes\Sym^{d-3}\mathcal{V}^{\vee}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">By taking first Chern classes, we see that <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}=\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}=\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> (recall the <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> classes defined in (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2. Tautological rings ‣ 2. Preliminaries on the tautological ring ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>)). Taking higher Chern classes and using the splitting principle shows that <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}(\mathcal{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}(\mathcal{V})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{3}(\mathcal{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{3}(\mathcal{V})</annotation></semantics></math> are also polynomials in the <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> classes.
Meanwhile, pulling back by <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}^{*}\omega_{f}=\eta_{i}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d-3)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{X}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}^{*}\omega_{f}=\eta_{i}^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{V}}(d-3)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{X}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Taking first Chern classes, we see that
<math id="S7.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i}=(d-3)z_{i}+\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i}=(d-3)z_{i}+\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=\frac{1}{d-3}(\psi_{i}-\lambda_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=\frac{1}{d-3}(\psi_{i}-\lambda_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. (Note that we are using <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-3\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-3\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.) The result now follows by Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 7.3. ‣ 7.2. Generators for the Chow ring ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 7.5</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S7.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 11</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{3,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{3,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Corollary 1.1 of []). ‣ 6. Genus 2 and hyperelliptic curves in general ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>, we know all classes supported on <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hyp_{3,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hyp_{3,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are tautological (the fundamental class is tautological by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, Proposition 1]</cite>; then use the push-pull formula.)
Moreover, <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hyp_{3,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hyp_{3,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP, as discussed in Section <a href="#S6" title="6. Genus 2 and hyperelliptic curves in general ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. By excision, it remains to show that <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{3,n}\smallsetminus\Hyp_{3,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{3,n}\smallsetminus\Hyp_{3,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Every curve in <math id="S7.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{3,n}\smallsetminus\Hyp_{3,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{3,n}\smallsetminus\Hyp_{3,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="S7.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-pointed plane quartic, so <math id="S7.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{3,n}\smallsetminus\Hyp_{3,n}\cong\mathcal{F}_{4,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{3,n}\smallsetminus\Hyp_{3,n}\cong\mathcal{F}_{4,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S7.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{4,n}\rightarrow\mathcal{F}_{4,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{4,n}\rightarrow\mathcal{F}_{4,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>-banded gerbe, we see that by combining Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm6" title="Lemma 3.6. ‣ 3.1. Basic lemmas ‣ 3. The Chow–Künneth generation property ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> with Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 7.2. ‣ 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, <math id="S7.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{3,n}\smallsetminus\Hyp_{3,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{3,n}\smallsetminus\Hyp_{3,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP. Moreover, by Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 7.4. ‣ 7.2. Generators for the Chow ring ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a>, it has <math id="S7.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.3. </span>Conclusion for <math id="S7.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=3</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Corollary <a href="#S7.Thmthm5" title="Corollary 7.5. ‣ 7.2. Generators for the Chow ring ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a> gives us a new column of open circles in genus <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, pictured in the left chart below. By the first version of the filling criterion, Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Filling criterion, version 1). ‣ 4. Filling criteria ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we can immediately fill in the circles with <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 7</annotation></semantics></math>, pictured in the middle chart below. With some extra work, we show in Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 7.8. ‣ 7.3. Conclusion for 
          
            
              =
              g
              3 ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.8</span></a> that we can also fill in the additional circle where <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=8</annotation></semantics></math>, pictured on the right.</p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="273.7" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 184.24 273.7" width="184.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,273.7) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(16.79,0) translate(0,40.11)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.5 0.0 0.0 0.5 14.02 -13.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.5 0.0 0.0 0.5 29.77 -13.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.5 0.0 0.0 0.5 45.51 -13.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.5 0.0 0.0 0.5 61.26 -13.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.5 0.0 0.0 0.5 -12.75 13.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.5 0.0 0.0 0.5 -12.75 29.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.5 0.0 0.0 0.5 -12.75 45.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.5 0.0 0.0 0.5 -12.75 60.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"