<foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:4.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="67.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.SS3.p1.pic3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Lemma 7.8</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The reason <math id="S7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g,n)=(3,8)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g,n)=(3,8)</annotation></semantics></math> is not already filled is because</p>
<ol id="S7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Filling criterion, version 1). ‣ 4. Filling criteria ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>(3) is not satisfied because the circle for <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g-1,n+2)=(2,10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g-1,n+2)=(2,10)</annotation></semantics></math> is not filled. In turn, the reason that the circle at <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,10)</annotation></semantics></math> is not filled is that:</p>
<ol id="S7.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Filling criterion, version 1). ‣ 4. Filling criteria ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>(2) fails for <math id="S7.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g-2,n+1)=(1,11)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g-2,n+1)=(1,11)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Filling criterion, version 1). ‣ 4. Filling criteria ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>(3) fails for <math id="S7.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g-1,n+2)=(1,12)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g-1,n+2)=(1,12)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the following four stable graphs</p>
<table id="S7.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{1,11}\times\mathcal{M}_{0,3}\qquad\qquad\quad\mathcal{M}_{1,12}\qquad\qquad\mathcal{M}_{2,10}\qquad\qquad\mathcal{M}_{3,8}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:5em;" width="5em"></mspace><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msub><mspace style="width:4em;" width="4em"></mspace><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mspace style="width:4em;" width="4em"></mspace><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{1,11}\times\mathcal{M}_{0,3}\qquad\qquad\quad\mathcal{M}_{1,12}\qquad\qquad\mathcal{M}_{2,10}\qquad\qquad\mathcal{M}_{3,8}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.2" class="ltx_logical-block">
        
<div id="S7.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para"><img src="2208.02357v2/SamsStableGraphs_1.png" id="S7.SS3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="499" height="121" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
<p id="S7.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">The graphs corresponding to the “unfilled” strata in <math id="S7.SS3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
      
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We claim that all other strata of <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math>
lie in the image of some <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g_{i},n_{i}}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∏</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g_{i},n_{i}}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math> where the vertices for <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{i},n_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{i},n_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> are already filled (i.e. <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}\leq 9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}\leq 9</annotation></semantics></math>; or <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}\leq 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}\leq 7</annotation></semantics></math>.)
Indeed, if <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is in the stable graph stratification for <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math>, then all vertices of <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy
<math id="S7.SS3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g(v)+n(v)\leq 14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g(v)+n(v)\leq 14</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, the only <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g,n)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g+n\leq 14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g+n\leq 14</annotation></semantics></math> which are not already filled
are</p>
<table id="S7.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,11)\qquad(1,12)\qquad(2,10)\qquad(3,8)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,11)\qquad(1,12)\qquad(2,10)\qquad(3,8).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">For the latter three, there is only one stable graph that uses such a vertex, which is the one pictured in (<a href="#S7.E3" title="In 7.3. Conclusion for 
          
            
              =
              g
              3 ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>). For <math id="S7.SS3.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,11)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,11)</annotation></semantics></math> there are a few stable graphs:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para"><img src="2208.02357v2/SamsStableGraphs4.png" id="S7.SS3.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="499" height="141" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">However, all but the first one appear in the image of <math id="S7.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,9}\times\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{2,9}\times\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math> because they have a disconnecting node (corresponding to the edge with a red dashed line through it above).</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\circ}=\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{2}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{3}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\circ}=\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{2}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{3}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{4}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the union of the four strata in (<a href="#S7.E3" title="In 7.3. Conclusion for 
          
            
              =
              g
              3 ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>). Note that <math id="S7.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\circ}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\circ}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math> is open as the set of graphs is closed under taking edge contractions. (In fact, each stratum above lies in the closure of the one to its right: <math id="S7.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma_{1}}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma_{2}}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma_{3}}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma_{4}}=\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma_{1}}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma_{2}}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma_{3}}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma_{4}}=\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>.) It remains to show that <math id="S7.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S7.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We do this by cutting <math id="S7.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> into two pieces.
Let <math id="S7.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> be the open locus where the dualizing sheaf is very ample and let <math id="S7.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> be the closed complement of <math id="S7.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.6</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have <math id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and all classes supported on <math id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> are tautological in <math id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We shall show that <math id="S7.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\cap\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{i}}=\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\cap\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{i}}=\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S7.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">(<math id="S7.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math>) Curves in <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> are reducible, so <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>.
We must show <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\cap\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\cap\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> too.
Suppose <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=E\cup L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=E\cup L</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> genus <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> genus <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},p_{2},p_{3}\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},p_{2},p_{3}\in E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1},q_{2},q_{3}\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1},q_{2},q_{3}\in L</annotation></semantics></math> be the points above the nodes (see Figure <a href="#S7.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Proof. ‣ 7.3. Conclusion for 
          
            
              =
              g
              3 ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, left).
Then</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}|_{E}=\omega_{E}(p_{1}+p_{2}+p_{3})=\mathcal{O}_{E}(p_{1}+p_{2}+p_{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}|_{E}=\omega_{E}(p_{1}+p_{2}+p_{3})=\mathcal{O}_{E}(p_{1}+p_{2}+p_{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is very ample on <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. Meanwhile,</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}|_{L}=\omega_{L}(q_{1}+q_{2}+q_{3})=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-2)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(3)=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}|_{L}=\omega_{L}(q_{1}+q_{2}+q_{3})=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-2)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(3)=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">is also very ample.
Hence, <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\omega_{C}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\omega_{C}|</annotation></semantics></math> is very ample and sends <math id="S7.SS3.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> to the union of a smooth cubic and a line.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2208.02357v2/both.svg" id="S7.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" width="449" height="218"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2. </span>Left: a curve in <math id="S7.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and its normalization. Right: a curve in <math id="S7.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{2}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{2}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math> and its partial normalization</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S7.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">(<math id="S7.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=2,3</annotation></semantics></math>) Next, let us describe the intersection of <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{2}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{2}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a curve in <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{2}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{2}}\cup\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider the partial normalization <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu:\widetilde{C}\to C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu:\widetilde{C}\to C</annotation></semantics></math> at one node.
Let <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> be the points lying over the node (see Figure <a href="#S7.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Proof. ‣ 7.3. Conclusion for 
          
            
              =
              g
              3 ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, right). Now, <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is an irreducible genus <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> curve.
We have <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu^{*}\omega_{C}=\omega_{\widetilde{C}}(p+q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu^{*}\omega_{C}=\omega_{\widetilde{C}}(p+q)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using this, it is not hard to see that <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to be very ample if and only if <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> are conjugate under the involution defined by <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\omega_{\widetilde{C}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\omega_{\widetilde{C}}|</annotation></semantics></math>. This is equivalent to <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> being in <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math> (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, Section 2.1]</cite>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">(<math id="S7.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=4</annotation></semantics></math>) The final stratum <math id="S7.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{4}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of smooth genus <math id="S7.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> curves. It is well-known that the canonical line bundle fails to be very ample if and only if the curve is hyperelliptic, so <math id="S7.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{4}}\cap Z=\Hyp_{4,8}=\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{4}}\cap\mathcal{I}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Hyp</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{4}}\cap Z=\Hyp_{4,8}=\mathcal{M}_{\Gamma_{4}}\cap\mathcal{I}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">To finish the proof, note that <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> is open inside <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 6.2 (Theorem 1.1 of []). ‣ 6. Genus 2 and hyperelliptic curves in general ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>, we see that <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and is generated by restrictions of tautological classes. The fundamental class
of <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{3,8}\cap\mathcal{M}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>
is tautological since it is the pullback under <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\circ}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\circ}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> of the closure of the hyperelliptic locus inside <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is tautological by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, Proposition 1]</cite>). Thus, we are done using the push-pull formula.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we study the open complement <math id="S7.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\subset\mathcal{M}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.SS3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{P}K_{4,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{P}K_{4,8}</annotation></semantics></math> be as in the previous subsection.
We consider the base change</p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S7.SS3.p15.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="68.57" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-34.29px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 95.21 68.57" width="95.21"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,68.57) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(47.6,0) translate(0,34.29)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -47.6 -25.26)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 68.57)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.06)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 2.43 0) translate(9.8,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.84 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.56em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.99" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="7.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p15.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\widetilde{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\widetilde{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 31.72 0) translate(44.72,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -5.55 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.8em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="11.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p15.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces Y}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 59.55)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(12.23,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -6.27 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="12.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p15.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces X}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 24.46 0) translate(51.98,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -12.81 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.57em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.82" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.86)" width="25.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.SS3.p15.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -35.37 13.89 L -35.37 -9.91"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -35.37 -10.19)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -25.29 22.69 L 16.49 22.69"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.77 22.69)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 28.84 13.89 L 28.84 -11.51"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 28.84 -11.79)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -22.86 -21.8 L 9.24 -21.8"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 9.52 -21.8)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.7</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The substack <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Y}\subset\mathbb{P}K_{4,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Y}\subset\mathbb{P}K_{4,8}</annotation></semantics></math> is open and <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Y}\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Y}\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>-banded gerbe.
Hence, <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">The map <math id="S7.SS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math> is open, so <math id="S7.SS3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Y}\subset X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Y}\subset X</annotation></semantics></math> is open, and hence <math id="S7.SS3.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Y}\subset\mathbb{P}K_{4,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Y}\subset\mathbb{P}K_{4,8}</annotation></semantics></math> is open.
The map <math id="S7.SS3.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS3.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>-banded gerbe over its image (induced from our base change <math id="S7.SS3.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BSL_{3}\to\BPGL_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>BPGL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BSL_{3}\to\BPGL_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>), so it will suffice to show that <math id="S7.SS3.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the image of <math id="S7.SS3.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, curves in <math id="S7.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> have very ample canonical.
To see that the image of <math id="S7.SS3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S7.SS3.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> we need to know that the following additional property holds: The images of the marked points under the canonical model impose independent conditions on quartics. In the irreducible nodal case,
the configuration of markings imposes independent conditions by Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 7.1. ‣ 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a> with <math id="S7.SS3.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=4</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S7.SS3.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\leq 3d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\leq 3d-1</annotation></semantics></math>. In the case of a cubic union a line with all markings on the cubic, the configuration of markings imposes independent conditions on cubics by Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 7.1. ‣ 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a> with <math id="S7.SS3.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=3</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S7.SS3.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\leq 3d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\leq 3d-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, these points also imposes independent conditions on quartics.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 7.4. ‣ 7.2. Generators for the Chow ring ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a> implies <math id="S7.SS3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(Y)=R^{*}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(Y)=R^{*}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>. An argument as in Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 7.2. ‣ 7.1. Construction of the stack ‣ 7. Plane curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a> shows that <math id="S7.SS3.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p">Using excision and Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Basic lemmas ‣ 3. The Chow–Künneth generation property ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, the previous two lemmas combine to give the following.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.8</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The union <math id="S7.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\circ}=Y\cup Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\circ}=Y\cup Z</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S7.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="S7.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,8}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S7.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8. </span>Faber–Pandharipande Hurwitz (FPH) cycles</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To access pointed curves of genus <math id="S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>, we use Hurwitz spaces with marked points. We will study degree three covers in Section <a href="#S9" title="9. Trigonal curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and degree four covers in Section <a href="#S10" title="10. Tetragonal curves ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. This section contains some preliminary results about push forwards of certain geometrically defined cycles, which hold for covers of any degree <math id="S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. In this section, we assume the characteristic of the ground field is <math id="S8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math>. In our main theorems, we shall only need results for covers of degree <math id="S8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, so this only excludes characteristic <math id="S8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2,3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>, Faber–Pandharipande study pushforwards to <math id="S8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> of cycles from
Hurwitz spaces of covers with specified ramification behavior. This gives rise to many examples of effective, geometrically defined cycles on <math id="S8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> that are tautological.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.1. </span>Hurwitz spaces with marked specified ramification</h3>

<div id="S8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a genus <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and a degree <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="S8.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{1},\dots,\mu^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{1},\dots,\mu^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>
be a collection of partitions of <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="S8.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g-2+2k=\sum_{i=1}^{m}(k-\ell(\mu^{i}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g-2+2k=\sum_{i=1}^{m}(k-\ell(\mu^{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is the length of the partition.
Faber–Pandharipande study the space <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, which parametrizes degree <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, genus <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> has marked ramification profile <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{1},\dots,\mu^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{1},\dots,\mu^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> marked fibers (and no other ramification).
For example, in the case all <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{i}=(2,1,\ldots,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{i}=(2,1,\ldots,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the space <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}((2,1,\ldots,1)^{2g-2+2k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}((2,1,\ldots,1)^{2g-2+2k})</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizes simply branched covers together with a marking of all of the points in the ramified fibers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The admissible covers compactification of this space, which they call <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{H}_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{H}_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, has a natural map <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho:\overline{H}_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})\rightarrow\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,\sum\ell(\mu^{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:\overline{H}_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})\rightarrow\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,\sum\ell(\mu^{i})}</annotation></semantics></math> by taking the stabilization of the marked source curve. Faber–Pandharipande prove that the pushforward of the fundamental class of <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{H}_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{H}_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> is tautological.
We might then consider the image <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> of this cycle in <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, after forgetting some subset of the marked points. When the composition</p>
<table id="S8.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{H}_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})\rightarrow\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,\sum\ell(\mu^{i})}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{H}_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})\rightarrow\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,\sum\ell(\mu^{i})}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">is generically finite onto <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[Z]\in R^{*}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[Z]\in R^{*}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Restricting to the locus of smooth curves we find:</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8.1</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If the map <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,\sum\ell(\mu^{i})}\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,\sum\ell(\mu^{i})}\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has generically finite fibers, then
the closure of the image of <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has tautological fundamental class.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 8.2</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,\sum\ell(\mu^{i})}\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,\sum\ell(\mu^{i})}\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has generically finite fibers, we will call the closure of the image a <em id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Faber–Pandharipande Hurwitz cycle</em>, or <em id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">FPH cycle</em>, for short. Lemma <a href="#S8.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 8.1. ‣ 8.1. Hurwitz spaces with marked specified ramification ‣ 8. Faber–Pandharipande Hurwitz (FPH) cycles ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.1</span></a> says FPH cycles are tautological.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 8.3</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although Faber–Pandharipande state their results over <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the main tool they use is equivariant localization for torus actions, which holds over arbitrary algebraically closed fields (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>).
Their results thus remain valid over any algebraically closed field of characteristic <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math> (taking the characteristic <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math> is needed to ensure that there will be no wild ramification so the Riemann–Hurwitz formula (<a href="#S8.E1" title="In 8.1. Hurwitz spaces with marked specified ramification ‣ 8. Faber–Pandharipande Hurwitz (FPH) cycles ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.1</span></a>) continues to hold).</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.2. </span>Our Hurwitz spaces</h3>

<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We find it more convenient to work with the pointed Hurwitz spaces <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizing degree <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, genus <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> distinct marked points <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\ldots,p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\ldots,p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and no restrictions on the ramification behavior of the cover.
(The marked points need not be ramification points, though they are not prohibited from being so.)
There is a basic fiber diagram</p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S8.SS2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="71.99" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-36px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 119.14 71.99" width="119.14"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,71.99) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.57,0) translate(0,36)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -59.57 -26.97)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 71.99)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.52)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(23.98,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -18.02 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="36.04"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 47.95 0) translate(52.2,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.03 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.88em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="26.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 62.97)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 3.47 0) translate(20.5,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -14.55 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="29.09"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{M}_{g,n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{M}_{g,n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 51.42 0) translate(48.73,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -9.56 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="19.12"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{M}_{g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{M}_{g}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -35.59 12.18 L -35.59 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -35.59 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -51.91 -2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="13.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\beta_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\beta_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -11.34 24.94 L 20.76 24.94"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.04 24.94)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 2.68 28.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="4.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 40.58 12.18 L 40.58 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 40.58 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 43.84 -2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="6.27"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -14.81 -23.51 L 24.23 -23.51"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 24.51 -23.51)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the closure of the image <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the locus of curves of gonality <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq k</annotation></semantics></math>. There are proper maps</p>
<table id="S8.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}^{\prime}:\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}\smallsetminus\beta_{n}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}^{\prime}:\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}\smallsetminus\beta_{n}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">along which we can push forward cycles. The image of <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the stratum <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> of curves of gonality exactly <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now translate the work of Faber–Pandharipande to show that push forwards of certain cycles along <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are tautological. First, on <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the cycle</p>
<table id="S8.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T^{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T^{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}:\text{$C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}$ has a point of ramification order $\geq a+2$}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mtext> has a point of ramification order </mtext><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}:\text{$C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}$ has a point of ramification order $\geq a+2$}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The subvariety <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{a}\subset\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{a}\subset\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{0}=\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{0}=\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> since every genus <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> cover of <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has a point of ramification.
Then, on <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="S8.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\{(C\to\mathbb{P}^{1},p_{1},\ldots,p_{n}):p_{i}\text{ is a ramification point of $C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}$}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mtext> is a ramification point of </mtext><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{(C\to\mathbb{P}^{1},p_{1},\ldots,p_{n}):p_{i}\text{ is a ramification point of $C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}$}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Each <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S8.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="68.03" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-34.02px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 157.61 68.03" width="157.61"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,68.03) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(78.81,0) translate(0,34.02)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -78.81 -24.99)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 68.03)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.52)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(10.95,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -5 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.99"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 103.07 0) translate(43.88,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -4.71 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 59.01)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 21.91 0) translate(57.19,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -18.02 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="36.04"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -56.62 22.96 L 56.64 22.96"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 56.92 22.96)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.31 26.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.52em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="7.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -56.62 15.63 L -17.54 -9.89"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.8373 -0.54674 0.54674 0.8373 -17.3 -10.05)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -33.59 7.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="6.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces f}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 57.2 15.78 L 18.04 -9.89"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-0.83624 -0.54836 0.54836 -0.83624 17.81 -10.05)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 40.64 -4.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="6.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\pi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -23.96 -20.2 C -44.06 -16.27 -56.75 -5.21 -63.22 13.63"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-0.32443 0.9459 -0.9459 -0.32443 -63.3 13.89)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -62.77 -16.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="10.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\sigma_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\sigma_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">be the universal diagram over <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\subset\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\subset\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the ramification divisor of <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S8.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[R_{i}]=\sigma_{i}^{*}[R]=\sigma_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\omega_{\alpha})=\sigma_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\omega_{f})-\sigma_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\omega_{\pi})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[R_{i}]=\sigma_{i}^{*}[R]=\sigma_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\omega_{\alpha})=\sigma_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\omega_{f})-\sigma_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\omega_{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">By slight abuse of notation, we shall also write <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[R_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[R_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{*}[T^{a}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{*}[T^{a}]</annotation></semantics></math> for the restrictions of these classes to <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}\smallsetminus\beta_{n}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}\smallsetminus\beta_{n}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The main goal of this subsection is to prove the following.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 8.4</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\ldots,i_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\ldots,i_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be a subset of distinct indices in <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+2\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+2\leq k</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the push forward <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta_{n^{\prime}*}([R_{i_{1}}]\cdots[R_{i_{j}}]\cdot\epsilon^{*}[T^{a}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n^{\prime}*}([R_{i_{1}}]\cdots[R_{i_{j}}]\cdot\epsilon^{*}[T^{a}])</annotation></semantics></math> is tautological.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">First let us reduce to the case <math id="S8.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{j}\}=\{1,\ldots,n\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{j}\}=\{1,\ldots,n\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Consider the fibered square</p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="105.98" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-38.29px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 341.15 105.98" width="341.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,105.98) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(170.58,0) translate(0,38.29)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -170.58 -29.26)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.57)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.81)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.7,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -53.75 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.75)" width="107.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}\smallsetminus\beta_{n}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}\smallsetminus\beta_{n}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 119.41 0) translate(91.88,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -52.72 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.75)" width="105.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,j}\smallsetminus\beta_{j}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{g,j}^{k-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,j}\smallsetminus\beta_{j}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{g,j}^{k-1})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 269.97 0) translate(52.2,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.03 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.88em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="26.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 67.55)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 19.27 0) translate(40.43,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -34.48 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.75)" width="68.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 136.76 0) translate(74.53,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -35.37 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.11em;--ltx-fo-height:0.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.75)" width="70.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{M}_{g,j}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,j}^{k-1},}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{M}_{g,j}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,j}^{k-1},}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -110.87 12.18 L -110.87 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -110.87 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -127.19 -3.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.02)" width="13.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\beta_{n}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\beta_{n}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -73.43 38.56 C 3.11 63.66 57.55 61.91 131.81 32.14"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.92819 -0.3721 0.3721 0.92819 132.06 32.04)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 24.41 60.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.82em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="11.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\epsilon_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\epsilon_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -50.89 24.94 L -18.79 24.94"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -18.51 24.94)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -37.27 30.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.39em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="5.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces q}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 40.71 12.18 L 40.71 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 40.71 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 43.97 -2.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.02)" width="11.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\beta_{j}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\beta_{j}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 99.66 24.94 L 131.77 24.94"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 132.04 24.94)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 111.1 17.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.71em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="9.78"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\epsilon_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\epsilon_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -70.16 -25.81 L -1.44 -25.81"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -1.16 -25.81)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.38 -33.23)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="5.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p4.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces p}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<p id="S8.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> forget the markings for indices not in <math id="S8.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\ldots,i_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\ldots,i_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From this, we see</p>
<table id="S8.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta_{n^{\prime}*}([R_{i_{1}}]\cdots[R_{i_{j}}]\cdot\epsilon_{n}^{*}[T^{a}])=\beta_{n^{\prime}*}q^{*}([R_{1}]\cdots[R_{j}]\cdot\epsilon_{j}^{*}[T^{a}])=p^{*}\beta_{j^{\prime}*}([R_{1}]\cdots[R_{j}]\cdot\epsilon_{j}^{*}[T^{a}])." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n^{\prime}*}([R_{i_{1}}]\cdots[R_{i_{j}}]\cdot\epsilon_{n}^{*}[T^{a}])=\beta_{n^{\prime}*}q^{*}([R_{1}]\cdots[R_{j}]\cdot\epsilon_{j}^{*}[T^{a}])=p^{*}\beta_{j^{\prime}*}([R_{1}]\cdots[R_{j}]\cdot\epsilon_{j}^{*}[T^{a}]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="S8.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves tautological classes, it suffices to treat the case <math id="S8.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we wish to show that the intersection <math id="S8.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})</annotation></semantics></math> is dimensionally transverse.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8.5</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The map <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\to\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\to\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> has finite fibers. In particular, every component of <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> and dominates <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">More generally, <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})\to T^{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})\to T^{a}</annotation></semantics></math> has finite fibers. Every component of <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+a</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> and dominates <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{a}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The fiber of <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> over a degree <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the finitely many ways to choose and label <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> distinct ramification points.
The map <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}\to\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}\to\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> has relative dimension <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Being an intersection of <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> divisors, every component of <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> has dimension at least <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}-n=\dim\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\mathcal{H}_{k,g,n}-n=\dim\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because all fibers of <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\to\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\to\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> have dimension <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that every component of <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension exactly <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and dominates <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. The same argument applies over any subvariety <math id="S8.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{a}\subset\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{a}\subset\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S8.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 8.4. ‣ 8.2. Our Hurwitz spaces ‣ 8. Faber–Pandharipande Hurwitz (FPH) cycles ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S8.Thmthm5" title="Lemma 8.5. ‣ 8.2. Our Hurwitz spaces ‣ 8. Faber–Pandharipande Hurwitz (FPH) cycles ‣ On the Chow and cohomology rings of moduli spaces of stable curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.5</span></a>, the product of classes is represented by the class of the scheme-theoretic intersection</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[R_{1}]\cdots[R_{n}]\cdot\epsilon^{*}[T^{a}]=[R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[R_{1}]\cdots[R_{n}]\cdot\epsilon^{*}[T^{a}]=[R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">If all fibers of <math id="S8.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are positive-dimensional, then the push forward is zero, hence tautological. Let us therefore assume that <math id="S8.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{m})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{m})\to\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is generically finite.
Then the push forward <math id="S8.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta_{n^{\prime}*}([R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n^{\prime}*}([R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a})])</annotation></semantics></math> is some multiple of <math id="S8.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\beta_{n}^{\prime}(R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\beta_{n}^{\prime}(R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a}))]</annotation></semantics></math>, so it suffices to show <math id="S8.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\beta_{n}^{\prime}(R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\beta_{n}^{\prime}(R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a}))]</annotation></semantics></math> is tautological on <math id="S8.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We do this by realizing the closure in <math id="S8.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S8.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}^{\prime}(R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}^{\prime}(R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}\cap\epsilon^{-1}(T^{a}))</annotation></semantics></math> as an FPH cycle.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us first treat the case <math id="S8.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=0</annotation></semantics></math>, as it is simpler. Let <math id="S8.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{i}=(2,1,\ldots,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{i}=(2,1,\ldots,1)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S8.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,m:=2g-2+2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,m:=2g-2+2k</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S8.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\sum\ell(\mu^{i})=m(k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\sum\ell(\mu^{i})=m(k-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider the diagram</span></p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S8.SS2.p8.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="121.29" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-60.64px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 368.96 121.29" width="368.96"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,121.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(184.48,0) translate(0,60.64)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -184.48 -51.62)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 121.29)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.75)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 179.63 0) translate(75.68,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -36.51 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.28em;--ltx-fo-height:0.7em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.69)" width="73.02"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p8.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces R_{1}\cap\cdots\cap R_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 63.82)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(47.75,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -41.8 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.04em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="83.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p8.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces H_{g}(\mu^{1},\ldots,\mu^{m})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 95.51 0) translate(58.67,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.5 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.82em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="39"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.SS2.p8.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g,N}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 198.12 0) translate(57.19,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -18.02 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-siz